<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Guandu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">200</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Guandu was fought in 200 CE near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> between the warlords <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shao">Yuan Shao</a>. Though heavily outnumbered, Cao Cao won by raiding and burning Yuan Shao's supply depot at Wuchao. The victory made him master of northern China and laid the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-guandu.jpg" alt="Battle of Guandu" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guanduzhizhan.png: User Zhuwq on zh.wikipedia derivative work: Deadkid dk (talk) 02:40, 10 July 2009 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guanduzhizhan_eng.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
